{
 "scene_id": "01.3",
 "poem": "01",
 "title": "Out of Life",
 "movement": "THE FALL",
 "seconds": 13,
 "lines": "trip on my own words\u2014 / falling out of life / & find / where you go when you / leave. / It was the maze / constructed / by a tainted love / a known, yet unknown / pit\u2014beneath the / quicksands of the make-believe / haven\u2014 / & hidden in the / overnourished forests / of escapism / that calls for you\u2014 / at this age / I'll follow, falling / the full distance / between / us almost having / it all / & starting anew\u2014 / to rediscover / when love was real. / I've failed at / protecting you / from your own vices\u2014",
 "set": "city_fall_void",
